From 178139877c0237069f4f81426fcf1408863d83fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:45:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] book ch.18 part 2: GLM term selection, lack of fit and dose
 estimation

- glm_analysis: optional lack-of-fit factor for the covariate (Period in
  Example 18.4) with marginality (the covariate is marginal to it),
  marginal deviance tests of eligible terms, backward selection with the
  dispersion re-estimated in every model (Table 18.13), final-model
  analysis of deviance and predictions per covariate level.
- Dose for given probabilities (LD50 and others) per treatment group from
  the binomial model with Fieller limits, back-transformed to the
  original covariate scale; warning for non-parallel slopes (18.2.8).
- Tests against Table 18.13 and Examples 18.2B, 18.4; Fieller limits
  checked against the defining quadratic.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A2hqwsyFif9SnDnzK8co2e
